## Conversation
Feedback item 5: planner check prints advisories for every plan in the root on each run; a filter would keep the signal for the plan just edited. The feedback suggested `--plan <name>`; I used positional names to match get, tree, and describe.

## Actions
runCheck takes names, resolves them with findPlans, filters with findingsFor, and returns the missing-name error joined with the error summary when both exist. When every name is missing nothing is printed and only the missing error is returned, so "No findings." is not shown for a plan that does not exist. check gained cobra.ArbitraryArgs and plan completion. TestCheckNamedPlans covers a two-plan filter, a clean plan, an unknown name, and a found-plus-missing mix. Docs in README.md, CLAUDE.md, and the check help text.

